{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-ccbf462f543341143e1c","statement":"(1) Let $\\bA$ be a local $\\Mk$-algebra.\nThen $\\bA$ is nodal if and only if it is isomorphic to one of the following algebras:\n\n- The algebra $\\Mk [[x]]$ of power series.\n\n- The local ring $\\Mk [[x,y]]/(xy)$ of a simple node of an algebraic curve over $\\Mk$.\n\n- The dihedral algebra $\\Mk \\left<\\left< x,y\\right>\\right> /(x^{2}, y^{2})$.\n\n(2) Let $\\bA =\\Mk\\kQ/\\kI$ be a two-point algebra.\nThen the following conditions are equivalent:\n\n- $\\bA $ is nodal.\n\n- $\\bA $ is isomorphic to the completion of one of the algebras from Table <<ref:table_nodal>> below.","source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"b5a5d12980c783ce0968a6a75cf0924f52997f58b8fe23b22e272059ecd8e959","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 3","ref_key":"nodal","name":"","order":5,"deps":[{"ref":"table_nodal","card_id":null,"label":null,"resolved":false,"target":"statement"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"4691b7e6310aff594015f4ee9295f0c5d77eb87af5ba0a297bb3f4cdbb2ee258","line":335,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:07+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":555,"math_hints":40}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","title":"Derived tame local and two-point algebras","abstract":"We determine derived representation type of complete finitely generated local and two-point algebras over an algebraically closed field.","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Yuriy Drozd","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2008","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"lenght":"\\mathop\\mathrm{lenght}\\nolimits","md":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{mod}","pr":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{pro}","bp":"\\bullet","iso":"\\simeq","iff":"i